re() is called once per pass (one instance, one trailing save() — the impossible_links.py pattern) or per mutation, so the durability contract and per-pass file-I/O cost are unambiguous.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3533,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan API line: 'open_store(repo_root)', ... 'save()' — listed as surface but no caller/timing given","Edit 3 says only 'build the callback and pass it into update_one(...)' — silent on when the store is opened and saved","The callback shape (fired per accepted link ADD) invites a per-link save() unless the plan pins the save to pass scope","Sibling impossible_links.py opens once per pass (one store instance = one pass) and saves once at pass end — the plan does not state whether it follows that pattern"],"finding":"The plan specifies open_store()/save() as store API but never states the store's open/save LIFECYCLE — who opens it and when it is persisted (per-link-callback, per-mutation, or once per pass). This is a load-bearing mechanism decision left unstated: saving inside the per-link callback re-reads and rewrites the whole JSON file on every confirmed link (O(mutations x records) full-file rewrites per pass), whereas opening once per pass and saving once is O(records).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbf36290a0ea2c143","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope > 'Write seam (three edits, callback-shaped)' edit 3, and 'API' bullet","norm_id":"n82e66e54733a54b8","priority":0.4467,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A pass with many outbound UPDATEs each carrying link ADDs rewrites peer_confirmations.json once per confirmed link","An implementer chooses a per-mutation open (fresh load each time), so intra-pass records only accumulate because dispatch is serial — an assumption the plan never makes explicit"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add one sentence to edit 3 fixing the lifecycle, e.g. 'handle_update opens the store once and closes over it; save() is called after record() so a partway-through pass is durable' — or, matching impossible_links.py, 'one store instance per pass, saved once at pass end' — and note that intra-pass record accumulation relies on serial mutation dispatch.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the RETIRE/cleanup ownership for peer_confirmations.json — either name the story (e.g. S3/S4) that prunes records when a link is removed or a local id is retired, or note that stale-record cleanup is explicitly deferred with the rationale that stale confirmations are harmless.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T9","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Store file: '.tickets-tracker/.bridge_state/peer_confirmations.json' with record key '(source_local_id, target_local_id, relation)'","'Out of scope: ... the removal decline (S3), backfill (S4)' — removal is deferred but no story is named as owning confirmation-record cleanup","T9 requires a RETIRE/cleanup path for shared state that would otherwise leak/accumulate"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new persistent shared-state file (peer_confirmations.json) whose records accumulate but names no RETIRE/cleanup path: when a managed link is later removed, or a local id is rebound/retired, its confirmation record is never pruned, so the store grows monotonically and may retain stale confirmations keyed to dead (source, target, relation) triples.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f220f873cd9536196","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — store file and record key; Out of scope","norm_id":"nf77251de1322c3ee","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A local ticket is deleted or a relation is dropped; the peer_confirmations record for that pair is never removed, so the file accumulates orphan records across many passes."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a one-line note in Scope or Out of scope identifying who prunes peer_confirmations records on link removal / id retirement, or a rationale that accumulation is bounded/harmless for this additive story.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","s